# Environment variables — documented shape only (docs/10 §3; docs/09 §11).
#
# Tier 0 static launch needs NONE of these. Copy to .env.local for local
# dev; production/preview secrets live in the host's env store (Render).
# NEVER commit real values to git.

# ── Content source ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 'file' (default) reads content/site.ts — always works, no DB needed.
# 'db'   reads from PostgreSQL via Drizzle (requires DATABASE_URL below).
# CI always runs without CONTENT_SOURCE set → defaults to file mode.
# CONTENT_SOURCE=file

# ── Site URL — SEO/social metadata (pre-deploy hardening) ──────────────────
# Canonical URL for metadataBase (root layout), OpenGraph/Twitter card tags,
# and sitemap.ts. PUBLIC — safe to expose, it's inlined into the client
# bundle (NEXT_PUBLIC_*), not a secret. Defaults to http://localhost:3000
# when unset, which is fine for local dev.
# The real value isn't finalized yet (Render subdomain first, custom domain
# later), so it stays unset here — set it directly in Render's environment
# store once the production URL is known.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# ── Database (docs/09) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required when CONTENT_SOURCE=db. Use docker-compose.dev.yml for local dev
# (see repo root). Production value lives in Render's environment group.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://deepak:devpassword@localhost:5432/deepak_labs_dev

# ── Admin CMS auth (docs/27 §4, D-047 Option A) ────────────────────────────
# SESSION_SECRET: min 32 random bytes. Generate with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('base64'))"
# SESSION_SECRET=

# ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH: bcrypt hash of the owner passphrase. Generate with:
#   npm run admin:password --workspace=web
# (prompts with echo off, so the passphrase never enters shell history).
#
# IMPORTANT: in a .env file every "$" MUST be backslash-escaped, because Next
# runs dotenv-expand and would otherwise read "$2b", "$12" as variable names
# and silently truncate the hash — login then fails with "Incorrect
# credentials" even though the password is right. Quoting does NOT help.
#   correct:   ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH=\$2b\$12\$abc...
#   broken:    ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH=$2b$12$abc...
#   broken:    ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH='$2b$12$abc...'
# In the Render dashboard, paste the UNESCAPED hash — those values are stored
# literally and are never parsed as a .env file.
# ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH=

# ── Media storage — Cloudflare R2 (D-049, docs/28 §6) ──────────────────────
# Required only to upload images/PDFs from the admin. The public site reads
# media via MEDIA_PUBLIC_BASE_URL. All four R2_* values are SECRETS (env only,
# never committed). See README → "Media / R2 setup" for bucket + CORS steps.
# R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# R2_BUCKET=deepak-labs-media
# Public origin for reads (the bucket's r2.dev URL or a custom domain).
# NOT a secret — it is the public asset host. Empty → media features stay off.
# MEDIA_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://pub-xxxxxxxx.r2.dev

# ── AI / Dex v2 — grounded generation (D-059, docs/31) ─────────────────────
# SECRET. Empty → Dex silently stays on v1 cached recall; the site still works.
# Free tier: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey (no card, no billing account).
# LLM_API_KEY=
#
# Both optional — defaults target Google's OpenAI-compatible endpoint.
# Switching provider (OpenRouter, Groq, Cerebras, Mistral) is these two lines
# plus the key. No code change: the client speaks OpenAI chat-completions.
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai
# LLM_MODEL=gemini-3.1-flash-lite
#
# Kill switch. Set to "false" to force v1 cached recall with a valid key still
# in place — the rollback lever if generated answers regress in production.
# DEX_LLM_ENABLED=true
#
# Shared daily ceiling on LLM-backed answers, enforced durably in Redis
# (below). Defaults to 300 if unset — see docs/31 §2 for why, against
# Google's free-tier ~1,500/day.
# DEX_LLM_DAILY_LIMIT=300
#
# Reserved. Dex v2 sends the whole 43-card corpus in-context (~9k tokens), so
# no embedding/vector step exists yet — see docs/31 §3.2 for when that changes.
# EMBEDDING_API_KEY=

# ── Dex v2 abuse guard (D-060, docs/31) ─────────────────────────────────────
# SECRET both. REQUIRED for the LLM path to run at all — without these,
# getDexLlmConfig() refuses to enable v2 even with a valid LLM_API_KEY, because
# there would be no durable way to enforce the rate/budget guardrails below.
# Free tier: https://upstash.com (no card), create a Redis database, copy the
# REST URL + token from its dashboard.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
#
# Cloudflare Turnstile — human check gating the LLM path specifically (the v1
# cached path stays reachable without it). Free, unlimited, no card:
# https://dash.cloudflare.com → Turnstile → Add widget → mode "Managed".
# Site key is public by design (ships in the client bundle); secret key is not.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=

# ── GitHub sync (D-010) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
